"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14420) [\\#14421](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/14421)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:69
msgid ""
"S3 binary cache operations now happen via HTTP, leveraging `libcurl`'s "
"native AWS SigV4 authentication instead of the AWS C++ SDK, providing "
"significant improvements:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:71
msgid ""
"**Reduced memory usage**: Eliminates memory buffering issues that caused "
"segfaults with large files"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:72
msgid ""
"**Fixed upload reliability**: Resolves AWS SDK chunking errors "
"(`InvalidChunkSizeError`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:73
msgid ""
"**Lighter dependencies**: Uses lightweight `aws-crt-cpp` instead of full "
"`aws-cpp-sdk`, reducing build complexity"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:75
msgid ""
"The new implementation requires curl >= 7.75.0 and `aws-crt-cpp` for "
"credential management."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:77
msgid ""
"All existing S3 URL formats and parameters remain supported, however the "
"store settings for configuring multipart uploads have changed:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:79
msgid ""
"**`multipart-upload`** (default: `false`): Enable multipart uploads for "
"large files. When enabled, files exceeding the multipart threshold will be "
"uploaded in multiple parts."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:81
msgid ""
"**`multipart-threshold`** (default: `100 MiB`): Minimum file size for using "
"multipart uploads. Files smaller than this will use regular PUT requests. "
"Only takes effect when `multipart-upload` is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:83
msgid ""
"**`multipart-chunk-size`** (default: `5 MiB`): Size of each part in "
"multipart uploads. Must be at least 5 MiB (AWS S3 requirement). Larger chunk "
"sizes reduce the number of requests but use more memory."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:85
msgid ""
"**`buffer-size`**: Has been replaced by `multipart-chunk-size` and is now an "
"alias to it."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:87
msgid ""
"Note that this change also means Nix now supports S3 binary cache stores "
"even if built without `aws-crt-cpp`, but only for public buckets which do "
"not require authentication."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:89
msgid ""
"S3 URLs now support object versioning via `versionId` parameter [\\#13955]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/13955) [\\#14274](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/14274)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:91
msgid ""
"S3 URLs now support a `versionId` query parameter to fetch specific versions "
"of objects from S3 buckets with versioning enabled. This allows pinning to "
"exact object versions for reproducibility and protection against unexpected "
"changes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:96
msgid ""
"```\n"
"s3://bucket/key?region=us-east-1&versionId=abc123def456\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:100
msgid ""
"S3 binary cache stores now support storage class configuration [\\#7015]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/7015) [\\#14464](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/14464)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:102
msgid ""
"S3 binary cache stores now support configuring the storage class for "
"uploaded objects via the `storage-class` parameter. This allows users to "
"optimize costs by selecting appropriate storage tiers based on access "
"patterns."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:104
msgid "Example usage:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:107
msgid "# Use Glacier storage for long-term archival\n"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:108
msgid "'s3://my-bucket?storage-class=GLACIER'"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:110
msgid "# Use Intelligent Tiering for automatic cost optimization\n"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:111
msgid "'s3://my-bucket?storage-class=INTELLIGENT_TIERING'"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:114
msgid ""
"The storage class applies to both regular uploads and multipart uploads. "
"When not specified, objects use the bucket's default storage class."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:116
msgid ""
"See the [S3 storage classes documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/"
"AmazonS3/latest/userguide/storage-class-intro.html) for available storage "
"classes and their characteristics."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:119
msgid "Store path info JSON format changes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:121
msgid ""
"The JSON format emitted by `nix path-info --json` has been updated to a new "
"version with improved structure."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.33.md:123
msgid ""
"To maintain compatibility, `nix path-info --json` now requires a `--json-"
"format` flag to specify the output format version. Using `--json` without `--"
"json-format` is deprecated and will become an error in a future release. For "
"now, it defaults to version 1 with a warning, for a smoother migration."
msgstr ""

